# Sku dev repo — keep code under version control, leave bulky release assets
# on disk only (the addon folder is symlinked into WoW's AddOns, so these
# files must remain present locally; they just don't belong in git).

# === Binary assets (audio, fonts, images) ===
*.mp3
*.ogg
*.wav
*.ttf
*.otf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.tga
*.blp
*.xlsx

# === Generated game-data tables ===
# These ARE tracked (since 2026-08-21). They are generated, not hand-edited, but
# they are Lua TEXT: git deltas them extremely well, and the whole 136 MB tree
# costs ~27 MB of pack, a commit that does not touch them costs 0, and an
# ordinary data edit costs single-digit KB. A full regeneration that restructures
# a file (e.g. the per-section _wrap_deferred.py wrap) costs ~1.3 MB - once.
# What we buy for that: the shipped data and the code that reads it can no longer
# drift apart unseen. SkuDeferredData.lua asks for builder globals BY NAME; when
# a data file did not define them there was no diff to catch it, only a tester
# reporting an empty list. Keep them in.
# The genuinely expensive assets stay out, above: 118 MB of mp3 in 12,618 files.
# Already-compressed binary cannot be deltaed or zlibbed, so it costs full size
# in history and full size again on every re-encode. Those ship in the release
# ZIPs, which are separate storage and do not count against the repo at all.
# Generator scratch (*.bak, *.bak.old) stays ignored - see the section below.

# === OS / editor cruft ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.bak
# _wrap_deferred.py --rebak keeps the superseded backup here
*.bak.old
